A||||13||Carrolles||Ideas for GT Gauge Cluster||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||12-06-1999||04:42 PM||||I picked up an auxilary gauge cluster at the U-Pull-It lot today for $15 along with the console and brackets and was thinking about using it in my 85SE.<P>Cliff.  Have you thought about offering a digital display just for this cluster?  It could be used for just about anything, for instance a boost gauge for turbos and superchargers, or volt meter for the 85s that don't have one already.<P>I also picked up two perfect SE sail panels for $10 each.<P>I'm looking for wire connectors to mount to my power window switches.  I'd like the correct connector instead of using individual spade connectors for each conductor.  The Helms manual lists numbers for the connector but I haven't had any luck finding any yet.<P>Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||12-06-1999||05:19 PM||||Read your question wrong<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 12-06-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||12-06-1999||10:42 PM||||Carrolles, on the ralley gauge side looking at the harness plug, is the brown wire on the far right side and the gray wire on the far left side? If you got all your stuff handy there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ggarsk||12-07-1999||02:22 AM||||Carrolles,Batboy beat to the question. I have a rally guage set with no wiring plug. Any description on the wires would be greatly appreciated. Thanks, Glenn||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||12-07-1999||06:59 AM||||Hi,<P>This set is out of an 86 model.<BR>Looking at the plug that is attached to the gauge (not the plug on the cross chassis wiring harness that it plugs into):<P>The plug is rectangular with 8 slots arranged with two rows of four meaning four across the top and four across the bottom.  By the bottom I mean the side of the plug with the locking tab.<P>____________________<BR>|                   || H    G    F    E  |<BR>|                   |<BR>| D    C    B    A  |<BR>|                   |<BR>---------------------<BR>       [---]<P><BR>I'm not sure if this diagram will come out the way I intend so I'll describe it also.<P>Top row, left to right looking at the face of the plug:<P>H (black)  G (blank)  F (grey) E (blank)<P>Bottom row left to right:<P>D (Red/blk) C (tan) B ( blank) A (brown)<BR>    stripe<P>        [locking tab]<P>Hope this helps.  If not clear ask away.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||12-07-1999||07:03 AM||||Well I was right the diagram did not come out as I intended.<P>D is a red wire with a black stripe.<P>The locking tab is centered on the bottom side.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||12-07-1999||05:02 PM||||would you be able to take a picture of the plug?||||reg||5
Z||000007||Carrolles||12-08-1999||07:48 AM||||I attached a picture to an e-mail sent to the address listed in your profile.  It's not very good quality but it may help a little.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||ggarsk||12-08-1999||10:08 AM||||Boy,this makes me wonder how many different off the shelf components Pontiac used. My gauge cluster has 8 pins in a straight line. It is out of and'86. If you could send me a pic,maybe with that and the wiring examples posted here I can figure out how to wire it. Thanks,Glenn||||reg||1
Z||000009||ggarsk||12-08-1999||10:08 AM||||Boy,this makes me wonder how many different off the shelf components Pontiac used. My gauge cluster has 8 pins in a straight line. It is out of an'86. If you could send me a pic,maybe with that and the wiring examples posted here I can figure out how to wire it. Thanks,Glenn||||reg||1
Z||000010||Carrolles||12-08-1999||05:06 PM||||I gave you the info on the connector that is on the wiring pigtail about 12" long.  I didn't realize you were asking about the plug on the gauge itself.  Sorry.<BR>I'll take a look at it after work and get back to you.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Carrolles||12-08-1999||05:34 PM||||Ok I think I have what you want now.  I took a walk out to the parking lot and saw that the gauge set in deed has an 8 prong connector on it.  <BR>With the gauges laying on their back with the faces facing up and looking at the connector.  The locking tab on the connector is on the top.<P>There are eight pins in a single row.  Left to right they are:<P>blank,blank,blank,blank,grey,black,tan,red/blk-stripe,brown.<P>Sorry for the confusion.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||ggarsk||12-08-1999||07:08 PM||||That is just what I needed. Thanks Carrolles! ||||reg||1
Z||000013||batboy||12-08-1999||07:35 PM||||I thank you too Carrolles, now I don't have to disassemble mine again to check.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
